            description: "Fruit Notes describes Triple Crown as the last USDA-ARS release and notes that it is renowned for exceptional flavor, with some considering it the best-tasting eastern US blackberry. Source notes: moderate to high yield, adequate Mid-Atlantic hardiness though perhaps less hardy than Chester Thornless, earlier ripening than Chester Thornless, insufficient firmness for shipping, and strong suitability for local markets with short holding times and pick-your-own"
