            description: "Fruit Notes says that if growers consider one Arkansas blackberry, they should consider Ouachita. Source notes: successful coast to coast in the United States, unconfirmed hardiness across the whole Mid-Atlantic, high yields of high-quality 6 to 7 gram berries, 10 to 11 percent soluble solids, erect canes, broad adaptation, and a major role in expansion of the domestic shipping blackberry industry"
