            description: "Fruit Notes describes Navaho as the first Arkansas thornless blackberry and says some consider it the best shipping blackberry available. Source notes: medium 5 gram berries, moderate yield capacity, very good sweetness usually 11 to 12 percent soluble solids, good hardiness in the lower Midwest and some Mid-Atlantic areas, orange rust susceptibility, and erect canes"
