            description: "Fruit Notes describes Natchez as the newest Arkansas thornless blackberry release as of the article. Source notes: large long berries, eye-catching fruit on the vine or in clamshells, unknown hardiness for the Mid-Atlantic because it was released in 2007, about 9.5 percent soluble solids, and tartness risk if crop load is excessive in southern plantings"
